'''Connah's Quay Nomads Football Club''' ({{langx|cy|Clwb Pêl-droed Cei Connah}}<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://newyddion.s4c.cymru/article/26014|title=Cwynion wedi penderfyniad i ail chwarae gêm Cei Connah a'r Bala|date=22 January 2025|website=newyddion.s4c.cymru|language=cy}}</ref>) is a Welsh professional [[association football|football]] club based in [[Connah's Quay]], Flintshire. They play in the {{Welsh football updater|ConnahQ}}.

The club was founded in 1946 as '''Connah's Quay Juniors''' and adopted the '''Connah's Quay Nomads F.C.''' name in 1951. From 2008 to 2017, naming rights were controlled by gap personnel, a recruitment firm, and the club was consequently known as '''Gap Connah's Quay'''. The club's home ground is at Cae y Castell in [[Flint, Flintshire|Flint]], and accommodates 1,000 spectators.

For the 2006–07 season, they temporarily played their home games in [[Flint, Flintshire|Flint]] due to drainage problems with the [[Deeside Stadium]] pitch.

In April 2013, the club announced that starting with the 2013–14 season, they would be using an all red home kit, accompanied by an all yellow away kit to complement the new logo which includes the traditional colours used in the Connah's Quay Town crest.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.the-nomads.co.uk/news/2013/april/The-Nomads-launch-brand-new-look-for-2013-14-season/ |title=launch brand new look for 2013–14 season &#124; Dafabet Welsh Premier League |publisher=The Nomads |date=22 April 2013 |access-date=8 March 2016 |archive-date=20 December 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161220145107/http://www.the-nomads.co.uk/news/2013/april/The-Nomads-launch-brand-new-look-for-2013-14-season/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

On 2 March 2023 it was announced that from the 2023–24 season, they will play their home games in [[Flint, Flintshire|Flint]] due to behind the scenes tenancy problems with the owners of the Deeside Stadium. On 11 November 2025, the team announced plans to build a new 4000 seater stadium for themselves, Shotton Steel RFC, and potential International matches in both Rugby and Football.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Nomads Announce Quay Vision For Next Five Years With Stadium Plans {{!}} Connah's Quay Nomads Football Club |url=https://www.the-nomads.co.uk/news/2025-11-11/nomads-announce-quay-vision-for-next-five-years-with-stadium-plans/ |access-date=2025-11-12 |website=www.the-nomads.co.uk}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-11-11 |title=Connah's Quay Nomads announce plans for new stadium |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/articles/cvg7m7ed145o |access-date=2025-11-12 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref>"}}
